==Strategy==
This stage is a step up from its predecessors, in both difficulty and rewards, with its inclusion of many buffed threats on a timer to overwhelm the player through sheer DPS alone.

Despite that, a simple way to rush this stage is to spawn [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] as soon as the stage starts, followed by a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] once Jelly Dumpling Cat's [[Wave Attack]] farms the opening row of Cerberus Kids. You can then continue to spawn Cone Cats to protect Bahamut as he makes short work of the base. Since the base has relatively low HP, no enemies set as bosses, and the main threats spawning on timers, this stage is easily [[Cheese|cheeseable]] without having to ever fight the main threats.

Otherwise, the extreme stage length makes it difficult to advance meaningfully without confronting them. The only other strategy is to build a proper defense that will hopefully outlast the onslaught until the enemy waves have been exhausted.

As with any other [[XP Stage]], this stage offers large XP drops and yields a high amount on clear. If you are confident with your strategy, you should definitely bring a [[Battle Items#Treasure Radar|Treasure Radar]], [[Battle Items#Cat Jobs|Cat Jobs]], and [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Prof. Cat Jobs]] for his [[Good Jobs! (Combo)|Good Jobs!]] [[Cat Combo]]. And with all XP Stages, you'll be presented with the option to watch an advertisement to double the stage's base XP drop. Adding it all up, that's '''6 MILLION XP!''' [[XP Function|(Exactly 6,269,960 XP.)]]

===Recommended Units===
*[[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]]/Cone Cat: Specialist [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]] that boast defensive abilities against [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] threats, with Cat Cactus even having [[Surge Immunity|Surge Immune]] to dismiss those spawned by Fallen Bear. They both work well with Research Effect UP [[Cat Combo|Combos]] to serve as your primary source of defense, but Cat Cactus is often preferred more due to its easier acquisition and slower speed that forms a thick line of defense.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Boulder's extreme health makes sure it stays for the brief moment it's there, and its [[Freeze Immunity|Freeze Immune]] prevents Cerberus Kids from paralyzing it. It should be used as a supportive option for defense, preferably aided by Research Combos to cover any gaps.
*Jelly Dumpling Cat: Jelly Dumpling's high damage and level 7 Wave Attack are essential for any strategy without a [[Rich Cat]]. It can be used to gather resources by killing the first Aku Doge and wipe out the swarm of Cerberus Kids, though without its true form it is of limited use later on for chip damage due to Aku Gory's presence, as your units will typically destroy the lower-ranged threats.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]]/[[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]]: Both are accessible [[Shield Piercing]] specialists that can greatly ease the fight against Fallen Bears with roughly the same consistency. Cat Researcher has the range to stay safe and doesn't rely on having to exploit [[Long Distance]], while Barrel's [[Area Attack|Area Attacks]], Surge Immune, and [[Resistant|Resistance]] to Aku threats can give it an edge if it manages to destroy several shields at once.
*[[Ancient Egg: N006 (Special Cat)|Fallen Bear Cat]]: An elusive unit that will likely only be used for replays, Fallen Bear Cat's [[Insane Damage]] to Aku and ability to outrange Aku Gory makes it a prime counter by greatly relieving your frontline pressure. It has no uses elsewhere due to its very low range, and as such ranged attackers are still required.
*Talented Awakened Bahamut: While this stage doesn't favor the use of such [[:Category:Melee-class Cats|Melee]] units, Bahamut notably sees use in cheese strategies. By exploiting the Aku Altar's low magnification and his guaranteed [[Explosion]] to easily defeat the starting Aku Gories, he can destroy the base quickly before the threatening enemies spawn.

===Recommended Ubers===
*[[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos]]: With Surge Immune, high range, being able to spawn Long Distance Surges herself, high survivability, and incredible DPS, there's not much more you can ask for in a unit to counter this stage. While she can't solo the stage, she definitely provides enough support to make things easier.
*Ultra Talented [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: Kai's over two million HP against Aku and ridiculous DPS allow her to act as an impenetrable wall against even the strongest threats of this stage. Dropping her into the frontlines will ease up some of the work of your meatshields, along with providing potentially devastating nuking capability.
*[[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Devil Hunter Satoru]]: A Long Distance [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|Crowd-Control]] unit whose main knack is [[Slow]] and [[Knockback]] with 50% chance to destroy [[Shield]]s, Satoru is an excellent supportive option for maintaining ground and allowing your other units to catch up. Surge Immune ensures Fallen Bear can't snipe him, and his very high effective range dramatically expands his effectiveness by hitting and destroying several Shields at once. Though beware of his somewhat large blind spot.

